# File: tests/bdd/features/texture_contact_sheet.feature
# Generated from: specs/152-add-a-contact-sheet-for-reviewing-generated-tiling-textures/requirements.md
Feature: Contact sheet for reviewing generated tiling textures

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Generate refreshes a root-wide contact sheet
    Given an output root holding the texture set "rusted-steel" with one albedo
    When a generate run for "oak-planks" succeeds with the fake worker
    Then the output root holds contact_sheet_001.png with 2 cells
    And the run's JSON result has contact_sheet with that page, cells 2, and no skipped entries

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Each cell shows the albedo tiled 2x2 with its name label
    Given texture sets "b-stone" and "a-wood" whose folders also hold _N, _R, and _compare.png files
    When the contact sheet is built
    Then the cells are ordered "a-wood" before "b-stone", then by backend and seed
    And each cell is its albedo repeated 2x2 under a label with the set name and the backend and seed
    And no derived map or comparison sheet is a cell

  @SCN003
  Scenario: The sheet command rebuilds on demand
    Given an output root with texture sets
    When "python -m nmg_game_dev.texture sheet --root <root>" runs
    Then it prints JSON with pages, cells, and skipped
    And it exits 0

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The texture_contact_sheet tool rebuilds on demand
    Given the texture-gen MCP server with NMG_GAME_DEV_TEXTURE_DIR pointing at an output root with texture sets
    When the texture_contact_sheet tool is called
    Then it returns pages, cells, and skipped
    And tools.json declares texture_contact_sheet

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Large roots page into numbered sheets
    Given an output root with 25 albedos and a stale contact_sheet_003.png
    When the contact sheet is built
    Then contact_sheet_001.png holds 24 cells and contact_sheet_002.png holds 1
    And both page paths are reported
    And contact_sheet_003.png no longer exists

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Unreadable albedos are skipped without failing
    Given an output root where one manifest lists a missing albedo and another lists a file that is not an image
    When the contact sheet is built
    Then both are listed under skipped with their path and reason
    And the remaining albedos appear as cells

  @SCN007
  Scenario: An empty root reports an error on demand
    Given an output root with no texture sets
    When the sheet command runs
    Then stderr has "ERROR [texture.no_texture_sets]" and a "Remediation:" line
    And it exits 1
    And the texture_contact_sheet tool returns the error code texture.no_texture_sets

  @SCN008
  Scenario: The rebuild needs no texture backend
    Given a host with no texture model weights whose hardware probe would fail
    When the sheet command runs on an output root with texture sets
    Then the contact sheet is built
